## Verdict

The Communication tab has a polished interface and a useful unified timeline, but it is currently closer to a communication logger with outbound sending than a production CRM inbox.

To become exceptional, it needs reliable message delivery, genuine inbound synchronization, threaded conversations, team ownership, compliance controls, and workflow automation.

## Critical issues to fix first

### 1. Make sending reliable

Email and Ooma delivery currently happen before the communication record is committed to the database in [communicationController.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/controllers/communicationController.js:73). Draft sending has the same problem at [communicationController.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/controllers/communicationController.js:101).

This can cause:

- A message being delivered but missing from CaseDesk.
- Duplicate messages when the browser retries.
- A message showing `Sent` without durable delivery evidence.

Implement:

- Save as `Queued` first.
- Transactional outbox table.
- Background delivery worker.
- Idempotency key on every send request.
- Retry with exponential backoff.
- Dead-letter queue for repeatedly failed messages.
- Unique provider-message constraint.
- Provider delivery-event history.

This follows the [AWS transactional outbox guidance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/cloud-design-patterns/transactional-outbox.html).

### 2. Build real inbound communication

Inbound currently appears to be manually recorded. IMAP status only checks whether environment values exist in [communicationProviderService.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/services/communicationProviderService.js:8); there is no mailbox synchronization worker.

Add:

- Google and Microsoft OAuth mailbox connection.
- Inbox synchronization and cursor/checkpoint storage.
- Ooma inbound SMS and call webhooks.
- Webhook signature verification and replay protection.
- Email bounce and rejection events.
- SMS delivery, failure, STOP and HELP events.
- Missed call, answered, transferred, voicemail and disconnected events.
- An “Unmatched communications” inbox when CaseDesk cannot confidently identify the client.
- Manual “Link to client/case” action.

Prefer OAuth over permanent app passwords. Google explicitly recommends Sign in with Google over app passwords, and Microsoft recommends Graph for new Exchange integrations. [Google guidance](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833?hl=en-GB), [Microsoft guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/exchange/client-developer/exchange-server-development).

Ooma supports call-flow webhooks for events including answering, transfer and disconnection. [Ooma webhook documentation](https://support.oomaenterprise.com/support/solutions/articles/48001238090).

### 3. Turn records into conversations

The schema has `CommunicationConversation`, but the composer never supplies a conversation ID in [CommunicationWorkspace.jsx](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/frontend/src/components/case-profile/CommunicationWorkspace.jsx:112). Consequently, the backend usually creates a new conversation for every message at [communicationController.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/controllers/communicationController.js:79).

Add:

- Threaded conversation view.
- Reply, Reply All and Forward.
- Email `Message-ID`, `In-Reply-To` and `References`.
- One conversation containing multiple messages.
- Conversation subject, participants, assigned team member and tags.
- Archive, reopen, mute and mark unread.
- Previous/next conversation navigation.

Those email headers are the standard mechanism for identifying replies and threads. [RFC 5322](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5322).

### 4. Replace hard deletion

Communication records are permanently deleted in [communicationController.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/controllers/communicationController.js:156).

For a legal CRM, use:

- Soft delete.
- Restore from trash.
- Retention policies by agency and record type.
- Legal hold.
- Restricted permanent purge.
- Immutable audit events recording who deleted, restored, exported or viewed something.
- Export history.
- Privacy-request export and redaction workflow.

PIPEDA guidance calls for access limitations, appropriate safeguards, and documented retention and destruction procedures. [OPC safeguards](https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/privacy-topics/privacy-laws-in-canada/the-personal-information-protection-and-electronic-documents-act-pipeda/p_principle/principles/p_safeguards/?wbdisable=true), [OPC retention guidance](https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/privacy-topics/business-privacy/breaches-and-safeguards/safeguarding-personal-information/gd_rd_201406/?wbdisable=true).

### 5. Add communication permissions

The routes currently use general authentication without communication-specific authorization in [communicationRoutes.js](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/backend/src/routes/communicationRoutes.js:6).

Create separate permissions for:

- View communications.
- Send email.
- Send SMS.
- Initiate calls.
- Export records.
- Delete or restore.
- View attachments and recordings.
- Manage provider connections.
- View communications assigned to other consultants.
- Send bulk communication.

## Essential CRM workflow

### Unified agency inbox

The current tab is case-specific. Add an agency-wide inbox containing:

- My inbox.
- Unassigned.
- Team inbox.
- Unread.
- Awaiting client.
- Awaiting agency.
- Failed delivery.
- Snoozed.
- Archived.
- Spam or blocked.

Each conversation should support assignment, watchers, internal notes, priority and response deadline.

### Composer improvements

Add:

- Editable and autosaved drafts.
- CC, BCC and Reply-To.
- Multiple recipients.
- Rich-text email.
- Attachments.
- Agency signature.
- Templates and reusable snippets.
- Case/profile merge fields.
- Scheduled sending.
- Send test.
- SMS segment and character counter.
- Preview before sending.
- Preferred client language and communication channel.
- Quiet hours and recipient timezone.

### Follow-up workflow

From any communication, allow:

- Create task.
- Add reminder.
- Schedule appointment.
- Request document.
- Update case stage.
- Assign team member.
- Mark “client response required”.
- Mark “consultant response required”.
- Record billable time.
- Add an internal note.

## Channel-specific improvements

### Email

- OAuth mailbox connection.
- Inbox and Sent-folder synchronization.
- Reply/forward/thread support.
- Bounce and complaint processing.
- Delivery-status timeline.
- Signatures, templates and attachments.
- Domain authentication health for SPF, DKIM and DMARC.
- Contact suppression and unsubscribe handling.

### SMS

Ooma requires business registration and a documented consent, opt-out and HELP process. [Ooma SMS requirements](https://support.oomaenterprise.com/support/solutions/articles/48001271312-requirements-for-sms-messaging).

CaseDesk should keep a consent ledger containing:

- Consent status.
- Consent source.
- Date and time.
- Purpose.
- Phone number consented.
- Proof or captured wording.
- Opt-out date.
- Resubscription evidence.

For commercial messages, CASL can require consent, sender identification and an unsubscribe mechanism, including for SMS. [CRTC CASL guidance](https://crtc.gc.ca/eng/com500/faq500.htm).

### Chat

Chat is currently reported as connected even though the UI polls every 15 seconds and appears to store ordinary communication records.

Implement:

- Actual Supabase Realtime subscription.
- Private case-specific channels.
- Row Level Security based on client/case membership.
- Typing indicator.
- Online presence.
- Sent, delivered and read receipts.
- File sharing.
- Offline notifications.
- Client portal chat interface.
- Message edit/delete policy.
- Reconnection and missed-message recovery.

Supabase recommends Broadcast for real-time messaging, with private channels and RLS authorization. [Supabase Realtime guide](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/getting_started), [authorization guide](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization).

### Calls

- Incoming and outgoing call synchronization.
- Call duration from Ooma rather than manual entry.
- Voicemail playback.
- Call disposition.
- Notes and follow-up task.
- Optional recording and transcription with consent controls.
- Link calls to appointments.
- Consultant time tracking.
- Unanswered-call queue and callback reminder.

Currently an initiated call can be marked `Completed` immediately, before CaseDesk receives the real outcome.

## Performance and usability issues

The frontend loads only 100 messages and then performs search locally in [CommunicationWorkspace.jsx](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/frontend/src/components/case-profile/CommunicationWorkspace.jsx:733).

Add:

- Cursor pagination or infinite loading.
- Server-side search and filtering.
- Search by sender, recipient, attachment, subject and message content.
- Date-range and status filters.
- Saved views.
- Bulk assignment, archive and mark-read.
- Database full-text search.

Additionally, polling calls `setLoading(true)` every 15 seconds at [CommunicationWorkspace.jsx](/Users/harvi/Emerks/casedesk/frontend/src/components/case-profile/CommunicationWorkspace.jsx:729), which can repeatedly replace the conversation list with skeletons. Background refreshes should update silently.

## Attachments

The database contains an `attachments` JSON field, but there is no complete secure attachment lifecycle.

Add:

- Drag-and-drop upload.
- File preview.
- Malware scanning and quarantine.
- File-type and size validation.
- Secure object storage.
- Per-case access checks.
- Expiring download URLs.
- Attachment audit history.
- Add attachment directly to Client Documents.
- Redact or remove an attachment without deleting the communication.

OWASP recommends validating actual file types, applying size limits, scanning uploads and storing files outside the public webroot. [OWASP file-upload guidance](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/File_Upload_Cheat_Sheet.html).

## Features that would make it exceptional

After the foundation is reliable:

- AI conversation summaries with human review.
- Automatic task and deadline extraction.
- Suggested replies based on case data.
- Translation with original and translated versions retained.
- Sensitive-data detection before sending.
- Response-time and SLA analytics.
- Unanswered-client-message dashboard.
- Consultant workload and communication-volume reporting.
- Template effectiveness and delivery analytics.
- Client communication preference centre.
- Automation rules such as “incoming document email → attach to case → notify consultant”.
- Conflict warnings when multiple staff reply simultaneously.

## Recommended implementation order

1. Outbox, background worker, idempotency and delivery events.
2. Inbound email, Ooma webhook ingestion and unmatched inbox.
3. Real threaded conversations and global agency inbox.
4. Consent ledger, retention, permissions and immutable audit.
5. Draft editing, attachments, templates, signatures and scheduling.
6. Proper Supabase client chat.
7. Call lifecycle, voicemail and follow-up automation.
8. Search, analytics and AI assistance.

The strongest product direction is to make Communication the agency’s operational inbox—not merely another case tab. Every message should reliably arrive, belong to one conversation, have an owner and response state, trigger work when needed, and remain securely auditable.